caption: Notebook

! Notebook

Settings for the Notebook theme.

!! Layout

<$radio tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-notebook/options/sidebarlayout" value="fluid-fixed"> Fluid story river, fixed sidebar</$radio>

<$radio tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-notebook/options/sidebarlayout" value="fixed-fluid"> Fixed story river, fluid sidebar</$radio>

> In ''fixed-fluid'' the story river keeps its width, so hiding the sidebar is composited entirely on the GPU — nothing reflows. In ''fluid-fixed'' the river reclaims the freed space, which is a layout change by definition; it is interpolated rather than snapped, so it glides, but it is not GPU work.

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-notebook/options/fullwidth" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="no"> Full width — story river and tiddlers take all the space the sidebar is not using</$checkbox>

> Full width lifts the cap on tiddler width and the 68-character measure on tiddler text, so tiddlers fill the story river. The sidebar keeps the sizing its layout mode gives it. In ''fluid-fixed'' the river takes the viewport minus the fixed sidebar. In ''fixed-fluid'' the sidebar is fluid and owns the space beside the river while it is visible, so the river only expands to the full viewport once the sidebar is hidden. On a wide display full width means lines longer than is comfortable to read, which is why it is off by default.

!! Paper

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-notebook/options/marginrule" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="yes"> Draw the margin rule down each tiddler</$checkbox>

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-notebook/options/ruleseditor" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="yes"> Rule the editor like notebook paper</$checkbox>

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-notebook/options/stickytitles" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="no"> Keep tiddler titles visible while scrolling</$checkbox>

